  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463578",
      "title": "Provide + Inject vs Props & Custom Events",
      "lectureOrder": 107,
      "videoOrder": 91,
      "sourceHash": "6f2c6a8d85cb0867cba127617fa4663f190e85d809101b1f6f651c32f31445c9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.66,
          "en": "So we learned about provide inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.66,
          "end": 6.55,
          "en": "in the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.55,
          "end": 10.01,
          "en": "And it is a very powerful tool built into vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.01,
          "end": 13.67,
          "en": "It's very useful for letting components communicate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.67,
          "end": 15.485,
          "en": "It's important for you to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.485,
          "end": 17.14,
          "en": "that you can only communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.14,
          "end": 19.63,
          "en": "between parent and child components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.63,
          "end": 22.8,
          "en": "or child components of other child components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.8,
          "end": 24.69,
          "en": "so that you can't use it to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.69,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "between neighbors or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 29.763,
          "en": "as I explained and showed over the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "But here's also one other important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "you should not always use provide inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 38.6,
          "en": "to replace props and custom events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.6,
          "end": 40.75,
          "en": "Indeed props and custom events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.75,
          "end": 44.53,
          "en": "should be your default communication mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.53,
          "end": 48.08,
          "en": "You might consider using provide inject though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.08,
          "end": 52.19,
          "en": "if you find yourself having some pass through components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.19,
          "end": 53.54,
          "en": "as we had it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.54,
          "end": 57.91,
          "en": "Knowledge base was just a component passing through props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.91,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "and passing through the immediate event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 63.52,
          "en": "In such cases using provide inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.52,
          "end": 66.41,
          "en": "can save you some unnecessary code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.41,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "and can make your code base a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 72.37,
          "en": "You could also argue that it makes a code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.37,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "a bit harder to understand though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 76.33,
          "en": "because if I look at this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.33,
          "end": 80.66,
          "en": "I see that I got two provided values here in App.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.66,
          "end": 83.94,
          "en": "but then I have to dig into all the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 87.37,
          "en": "to understand where those values are being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.37,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "This is absolutely doable in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 92.06,
          "en": "since it's not a complex app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.06,
          "end": 95.36,
          "en": "but it is something that can be cumbersome in bigger apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.36,
          "end": 97.63,
          "en": "So use it wisely.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.63,
          "end": 99.97,
          "en": "And if you have a lot of pass through components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.97,
          "end": 101.27000000000001,
          "en": "definitely use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.27000000000001,
          "end": 103.77000000000001,
          "en": "If you have just one pass through component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 107.44,
          "en": "you might still be fine with using props and custom events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.44,
          "end": 110.08,
          "en": "even though you have some redundant code though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.08,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "But that is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 114.93,
          "en": "and ultimately comes down to your personal preferences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 119.14,
          "en": "With provide inject and props and custom events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.14,
          "end": 120.78,
          "en": "you got all the core tools though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.78,
          "end": 123.74,
          "en": "which you need to let components communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.74,
          "end": 124.603,
          "en": "with each other.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
